# 1. What is Terraform?
“Terraform is an open-source Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool developed by HashiCorp. It is used to create, manage, and provision infrastructure such as virtual machines, networks, and databases using configuration files.
It supports multiple cloud providers, including AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud. Terraform helps automate infrastructure management, maintain consistency, and reduce manual errors.”
>Example: 
We can use Terraform to automatically create an EC2 instance, an S3 bucket, and a VPC in AWS.
> Key Benefits:
1. Automation: Creates infrastructure automatically.
2. Consistency: Uses repeatable configuration files.
3. Scalability: Makes it easy to manage multiple resources.
4. Version Control: Tracks infrastructure changes using Git.

# 1. Definition of Terraform
Terraform ek Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool hai, jise HashiCorp ne develop kiya hai.
Simple words mein, Terraform ki help se hum code likhkar AWS par EC2 instance, S3 bucket, VPC aur other cloud resources automatically create, update aur delete kar sakte hain.
Example: Agar humein AWS par 10 EC2 instances banane hain, toh manually banane ke bajay Terraform code se bana sakte hain.
# 2. History of Terraform
- 2014: HashiCorp ne Terraform introduce kiya.
- 2014: Terraform ka first open-source version release hua.
- 2021: HashiCorp ne Terraform 1.0 release kiya.
- Today: Terraform ka use AWS, Azure, Google Cloud aur other platforms par infrastructure manage karne ke liye hota hai.

